The equation κ = 
\frac{2π T_H}{Ι}
 relates the surface gravity of a black hole to its Hawking temperature and the reduced Planck constant. This formula specifically arises in the context of quantum field theory in curved spacetime, particularly when considering phenomena like Hawking radiation. It quantifies how strongly spacetime is curved at the event horizon, which is directly linked to the temperature at which the black hole emits thermal radiation.

